    "goal": "Characterize evaporation of a 9.72 µL hanging-drop screen at 10.3 °C and 63% RH over 2.012 h for an interior well (row D, col 5).",
    "rationale": "Hanging-drop evaporation follows the d²-law; the interior well (row D, col 5) has no edge enhancement (edge factor 1.0). At 10.3 °C / 63% RH the interior Langmuir evaporation rate is ~5.10 µL/h, leaving only ~1.57 µL of the 9.72 µL drop after 2.012 h — a ~84% volume loss that will concentrate solutes and risks desiccation. The drop is projected to fully dry in ~1.9 h, so the screen duration is too long for this drop size under these conditions.",
